# ============================================================================
# Agent repository .gitignore — SuperHermes normalised standard.
#
# MODEL: default-deny. The first rule ignores everything; the repo then
# re-includes ONLY the agent's durable identity — config, soul, memory, skills,
# scripts, crons, sandbox profile, and operating docs. Everything else stays out
# by construction: secrets, caches, logs, sessions, the Honcho Docker stack, the
# GBrain pglite store, isolated runtime homes, knowledge vaults, and third-party
# workspace clones. A brand-new kind of secret file CANNOT leak — if it isn't on
# the allow-list, it is ignored.
#
# This file is NORMALISED across the fleet (every agent follows this standard)
# but NOT CENTRALISED — each agent keeps its own copy at its root. Slug below is
# the only per-agent value. Regenerate from SuperHermes/templates/gitignore.tmpl.
#   agent slug: __AGENT_SLUG__
# ============================================================================

# ── 0. Deny everything by default ───────────────────────────────────────────
*

# ── 1. Repo control + top-level operating docs ──────────────────────────────
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/docs/
!/docs/**
!/memory/
!/memory/**
!/ops/
!/ops/**
!/workspace-index/
!/workspace-index/**

# ── 2. The Hermes profile — curated identity subset only ────────────────────
# Re-include each ancestor directory so git can descend, then the specific
# durable artifacts within. (Default-deny means every parent must be re-opened.)
!/.hermes/
!/.hermes/SOUL.md
!/.hermes/sandbox/
!/.hermes/sandbox/__AGENT_SLUG__.sb
!/.hermes/profiles/
!/.hermes/profiles/__AGENT_SLUG__/
!/.hermes/profiles/__AGENT_SLUG__/config.yaml
!/.hermes/profiles/__AGENT_SLUG__/honcho.json
!/.hermes/profiles/__AGENT_SLUG__/repos.yaml
!/.hermes/profiles/__AGENT_SLUG__/SOUL.md
!/.hermes/profiles/__AGENT_SLUG__/memories/
!/.hermes/profiles/__AGENT_SLUG__/memories/*.md
!/.hermes/profiles/__AGENT_SLUG__/cron/
!/.hermes/profiles/__AGENT_SLUG__/cron/jobs.definition.json
!/.hermes/profiles/__AGENT_SLUG__/scripts/
!/.hermes/profiles/__AGENT_SLUG__/scripts/**
# NOTE: profiles/<slug>/skills/ is deliberately NOT tracked. Skills are SHARED
# procedural memory — they live once in the shared skills library (referenced via
# config `skills.external_dirs`), not duplicated into every agent's identity repo
# (that tree is 600-900 files). If an agent authors a genuinely bespoke skill it
# wants versioned, allow-list that one path explicitly below.

# ── 3. Belt-and-suspenders: never track these even inside allowed trees ──────
# (Last-match-wins: these come AFTER the allow-list so they always win.)
# Secrets / credentials
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/auth.json
**/*google_token*
**/*token*
**/*credential*
**/*secret*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.kdbx
**/*.age
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/*.git-credentials
# Runtime state / locks / sessions / logs
**/logs/
**/sessions/
**/cron/output/
**/*.lock
**/*.pid
**/*.log
**/*.jsonl
**/gateway_state.json
**/processes.json
**/.usage.json*
**/.curator_state
**/.curator_backups/
**/.hub/
**/.archive/
# Memory/model binary stores (durable text lives in memories/*.md + vault, which
# is its own repo) — never the binary indexes
**/*.pglite
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.db
**/*.db-*
**/*.wal
**/*.shm
**/localmem_chroma/
**/chroma*/
**/*.gguf
**/*.safetensors
**/*.pt
**/*.pth
**/*.onnx
**/*.bin
# Caches / build / deps
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/node_modules/
**/.venv/
**/vendor/
# Generated media / archives
**/*.png
**/*.jpg
**/*.jpeg
**/*.gif
**/*.webp
**/*.mp4
**/*.mov
**/*.ogg
**/*.mp3
**/*.wav
**/*.pdf
**/*.zip
**/*.tar
**/*.tar.gz
**/.DS_Store
*.bak*

# ── 4. Big trees that never belong in the identity repo (clarity; already
#       covered by default-deny since they were never re-included) ───────────
# /.hermes/honcho/   Honcho Docker stack (cloned upstream, multi-GB)
# /.hermes/backups/  database dumps
# /.home/ /.cache/ /.npm/ /.local/ /.ollama/ /tmp/   isolated runtime + caches
# /vault/            knowledge vault — its OWN git repo, kept separate
# /workspace/        working area + third-party clones — never the agent identity
